# Explainer system (always on)

This repo makes VO-first Remotion explainers in the AI LABS production language.

Read before any scene work:

1. `docs/style/visual-system.md`
2. `references/ailabs/README.md`
3. Project skill `.cursor/skills/remotion-presentation/SKILL.md`

## Hard rules

- No talking head, no facecam, no lower thirds, no mascots in the body.
- Beat sheet first: `presentations/<slug>/beats.md`. No `Main.tsx` until it exists.
- Every beat is `diagram` | `mock` | `screencap`.
- Use only components listed in `docs/style/visual-system.md`. If you need a new one, add it to the kit and that list first.
- Proof screenshots are real files. Do not invent GitHub/X/docs UI.
- Cursor is synthetic (kit), never a raw mouse recording.
- Motion is data-driven (counters, progress, trees, status). No decorative-only motion.
- New video = new copy + new proof stills. Same chrome, tokens, easing.
- Tokens: `explainer` from `src/kit/theme.ts` for new explainers. Do not introduce a second palette.
- Primary ship format is 16:9 at 30fps (1080 to preview, 4K to publish).

## References

Watch `references/ailabs/clips/` when unsure. Match that language, not a generic tech-YouTube template.
